#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
"""lane-worktrees - one act that archives, rescues and removes a lane's
abandoned worktrees, branches, scratch and killed-suite sandboxes
(opensoft/openRepoTools#162).

    lane-worktrees sweep <lane> [--dry-run | --yes] [--porcelain]
                   [--bundle] [--branches] [--links]
                   [--include-scratch] [--include-caches] [--include-sandboxes]
                   [--include-foreign --word "<verbatim>"]
                   [--live <path> ... | --live none] [--fetch] [--estate <dir>]
    lane-worktrees sweep --expire [--dry-run | --yes] [--porcelain]
    lane-worktrees sweep --all --dry-run --report [--post <path|owner/repo#n>]
                   [--estate <dir>]
    lane-worktrees --help | --version

A SWAP THAT DOES NOT FINISH GRACEFULLY LEAVES ITS WRITERS' TREES WHERE THEY
STOOD, and the protocol's worktree-safety rule (a swap never commits, pushes,
stashes, resets or cleans) is right to leave them. This is the act that
retires them afterwards, in one place, with one rule: NOTHING IS DELETED THAT
IS NOT FIRST ON ORIGIN OR IN A BUNDLE under the sweeps directory, and a tree a
live writer owns is never touched.

THE DRY RUN IS THE DEFAULT and changes nothing - no fetch, no ref, no file,
no register line (`--fetch` asks origin first; `lanes-edit.sh`'s own reads
fetch the register as they always do). `--yes` performs the table, fetching
origin first in every repository it acts in.

WHICH TREES ARE THE LANE'S is #97's inventory (`lanes-edit.sh lane-trees`)
and the disk - never the derived index (Amendment 14 clause (b)). A tree the
inventory does not name is FOREIGN: reported, and left, unless
`--include-foreign` and a `--word`. A tree another lane's inventory names is
that lane's and is never acted on from here.

WHO MAY ACT is #97's reconciliation (`lanes-edit.sh lane-reconcile`): a lane
bound on another host or container is UNKNOWN, never dead (Amendment 18(b)),
so every act is refused for it; a lane held by another live session is
refused; a lane whose holder is THIS session acts only on the writer count
the coordinator states with `--live` (Amendment 17 Addendum 1 (i)).

"MERGED" is the register's LANDED line for the branch's pull request, or
`gh`'s MERGED state for it - never `git branch --merged` alone, because a
squash merge leaves no ancestry.

The sweeps directory: ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-$HOME/.local/state}/openRepoTools/
sweeps/<lane>/<UTC>/ with MANIFEST.sha256, DISPOSITION.md and rescues.tsv.
`sweep --expire` lists (and with `--yes` removes) archives older than the
retention (90 days; `sweep.conf`) whose every rescue branch is still on
origin at the rescued SHA; an archive whose rescue branch is gone or moved,
or that is not whole (its MANIFEST.sha256 missing or not matching, its
rescues.tsv unreadable), is never expired.

THE ESTATE REPORT (`--all --dry-run --report`) is the net under every actor
that never runs `lane-end`: FOREIGN clones, trees of ENDED lanes, unmerged
branches, root-`main` divergence, rescue branches and dirty trees awaiting
disposition, caches and sandboxes, large ignored directories, evidence-shaped
paths, archives past retention, the workspace's bytecode hygiene and
`status --all`'s findings - one markdown document, printed or `--post`ed to a
file or an issue. It changes nothing. `lane-start` runs it once a day per
workstation, detached (`LANE_WORKTREES_REPORT=off` is the switch). It exits 0,
or 1 when `--post` could not deliver it (the report is then printed).

`--yes` (and `--expire --yes`) is SWITCHED OFF until opensoft/openRepoTools
#170 lands: it is refused, exit 2, unless the environment carries
LANE_WORKTREES_ENABLE_YES=1 - which the test suite sets, and which is not for a
real estate until #170. The dry run, `--porcelain` and `--report` are whole.

PORCELAIN: one row per line, fields separated by one TAB. In every field a
backslash is written `\\`, a TAB `\t`, a newline `\n` and a carriage
return `\r`, so a path holding any of them is still one field of one row.
Undecodable bytes in a path pass through as the bytes they are.

Exit codes:
  0  dry run: nothing to retire  ·  --yes: every act completed
  3  dry run: something to retire (the `lane-end` gate's answer, #163)
  2  refused: the lane is bound elsewhere, held by another live session,
     managed-owned, has trees but no #97 snapshot, or a read failed - or
     `--yes` is switched off, or an error no read caught - nothing was changed
  1  --yes: an act failed part-way; what was done is recorded and the
     rest is left exactly as it was
 64  usage
"""

